==Strategy==
Due to how small the stage is, the Killer Axe Base is able to hit yours, meaning there is a soft timer to this stage. Bringing fast units, such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]], [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Talented Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] or [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Talented Can Can]] as well as anti-Dark crowd controllers such as [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] and 3-4 meatshields is highly recommended.

Essentially, the player has to rush this stage or cheese to be able to beat 11-15. CatCombos that affect the Worker Cat can be of use as money in these stages is tight, as the Doge Darks and Killer Cats are the only reliable source of income and the Killer Cats get increasingly beefy as stages go on.

Since the Killer Axe Base lacks immunities to Surges or Explosions, if one has [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat]], he can be used to deal serious damage to the enemy base if he's able to make it there, since all of the blasts from his Explosion will be able to hit. Support him with the abovementioned units, and you've netted yourself a free Dark Catseye.
